\section{Package ownership}{

Generic graph construction and algorithms belong to \code{dgraphs}; use its
current public help and object schemas. Examples include
\code{dgraphs::create.path.graph()} and \code{dgraphs::detect.graph.endpoints()}.
Adaptive extrema use \code{\link{detect.adaptive.extrema}} in gflow;
\code{dgraphs::detect.local.extrema()} is a distinct fixed-radius method.
Both packages share the \code{dgraphs::vertices()} generic.
Layout packages such as \code{grip} own their layouts. Generic 3D rendering uses
\code{ivue::plot3D.plain()}, \code{ivue::plot3D.cont()}, \code{ivue::plot3D.groups()},
\code{ivue::layer3D.path()}, and \code{ivue::layer3D.edges()}.
